# Oracle 11.2.0.2's reply to JDBC thin 11.2's `BEGIN SELECT c, b INTO ?, ? FROM t
# WHERE id = 1; END;`, a CLOB and a BLOB registered OUT (#2859): the I/O
# vector, then each LOB as its locator's length and the locator, then the status.
# Captured 2026-11-27 through tools/capture_proxy.py. The TTC payload,
# without the packet's header, as `hexdump -C` output; the offset column
# and the |ascii| gutter are ignored by tests.replay.parse_hexdump.
